      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T03:59:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`hasattr` works on any object and it checks if the given object has a given property. `in` only works on iterators, like list, dict.\n\nDouble checked that I actually don\u0027t need this check because the `devicetree.edtlib.Node` object must have the `parent` property. But the `parent` may be None if it is the root node so I need to check the None case before accessing `node.parent.name`.",
